ce_as_of":"page checked 2026-09-22","valid_from":null,"valid_to":null,"recorded_on":"2026-09-22","statement":"The UAE’s Abu Dhabi crude oil pipeline provides a route that bypasses Hormuz.","caveat":"Pipeline capacity must not be equated with unused capacity or actual flow.","review_status":"manually_source_checked_candidate","ground_truth":false},{"id":"O-C07","subject":"oil-china","predicate":"imports","object":"oil-crude","evidence_ids":["O-S05","O-S09"],"kind":"reported_trade","source_as_of":"2026-Q2","valid_from":"2026-04-01","valid_to":"2026-06-30","recorded_on":"2026-09-22","statement":"China imported an estimated 8.1 million b/d of crude oil in 2026-Q2.","caveat":"The 2026 figure is an EIA calculation based on customs data; it is not China’s total petroleum consumption.","review_status":"manually_source_checked_candidate","ground_truth":false},{"id":"O-C08","subject":"oil-china-refining","predicate":"consumes","object":"oil-crude","evidence_ids":["O-S06"],"kind":"official_statistic","source_as_of":"2026-06","valid_from":"2026-06-01","valid_to":"2026-06-30","recorded_on":"2026-09-22","statement":"China NBS reported 51.24 million tonnes of crude processed by above-designated-size enterprises in June 2026.","caveat":"The measure has a defined enterprise scope and remains in tonnes; no barrel conversion is implied.","review_status":"manually_source_checked_candidate","ground_truth":false},{"id":"O-C09","subject":"oil-china-refining","predicate":"located_in","object":"oil-china","evidence_ids":["O-S06","O-S09"],"kind":"reported_structure","source_as_of":"2026-06","valid_from":null,"valid_to":null,"recorded_on":"2026-09-22","statement":"China’s refinery system is distributed nationally and processes domestic and imported crude.","caveat":"A country-level industry node; no arbitrary refinery location is substituted.","review_status":"manually_source_checked_candidate","ground_truth":false},{"id":"O-C10","subject":"oil-us","predicate":"produces","object":"oil-crude","evidence_ids":["O-S08"],"kind":"reported_estimate","source_as_of":"2026-H1","valid_from":"2026-01-01","valid_to":"2026-06-30","recorded_on":"2026-09-22","statement":"EIA estimated U.S. crude production at 13.7 million b/d in the first half of 2026.","caveat":"The separate 13.8 million b/d full-year value is a forecast.","review_status":"manually_source_checked_candidate","ground_truth":false},{"id":"O-C11","subject":"oil-permian","predicate":"part_of_production_in","object":"oil-us","evidence_ids":["O-S08"],"kind":"forecast_context","source_as_of":"2026 forecast","valid_from":null,"valid_to":null,"recorded_on":"2026-09-22","statement":"EIA identifies the Permian as the principal region in its forecast U.S. production expansion.","caveat":"This is forecast attribution, not a measured share of every incremental barrel.","review_status":"manually_source_checked_candidate","ground_truth":false},{"id":"O-C12","subject":"oil-us","predicate":"exports","object":"oil-products","evidence_ids":["O-S07"],"kind":"official_statistic","source_as_of":"2026-04","valid_from":"2026-04-01","valid_to":"2026-04-30","recorded_on":"2026-09-22","statement":"U.S. crude oil and petroleum product exports reached 13.6 million b/d in April 2026.","caveat":"This total combines crude oil and multiple petroleum products; it is not crude exports alone.","review_status":"manually_source_checked_candidate","ground_truth":false},{"id":"O-C13","subject":"oil-opec-plus","predicate":"coordinates_production_policy_for","object":"oil-crude","evidence_ids":["O-S04"],"kind":"reported_decision","source_as_of":"2026-09-06","valid_from":"2026-10-01","valid_to":"2026-10-31","recorded_on":"2026-09-22","statement":"Seven OPEC+ participants announced that October required production would remain at September 2026 levels.","caveat":"A policy announcement is not evidence of subsequent production or conformity.","review_status":"manually_source_checked_candidate","ground_truth":false},{"id":"O-C14","subject":"oil-saudi","predicate":"uses","object":"oil-east-west","evidence_ids":["O-S02","O-S10"],"kind":"reported_rerouting","source_as_of":"2026-09-09","valid_from":null,"valid_to":null,"recorded_on":"2026-09-22","statement":"EIA reported Saudi rerouting through the East-West pipeline during constrained maritime flows.","caveat":"The pack does not quantify every rerouted barrel or establish unconstrained export capacity.","review_status":"manually_source_checked_candidate","ground_truth":false},{"id":"O-C15","subject":"oil-uae","predicate":"uses","object":"oil-uae-pipeline","evidence_ids":["O-S10"],"kind":"reported_structure","source_as_of":"page checked 2026-09-22","valid_from":null,"valid_to":null,"recorded_on":"2026-09-22","statement":"The UAE uses the Abu Dhabi crude oil pipeline as export infrastructure outside Hormuz.","caveat":"Structural capability does not establish actual period throughput.","review_status":"manually_source_checked_candidate","ground_truth":false},{"id":"O-C16","subject":"oil-malacca","predicate":"carried_flow_within","object":"oil-world","evidence_ids":["O-S11"],"kind":"estimated_flow","source_as_of":"2025-H1","valid_from":"2025-01-01","valid_to":"2025-06-30","recorded_on":"2026-09-22","statement":"EIA estimated total oil flows through the Strait of Malacca at 23.2 million b/d in the first half of 2025.","caveat":"A tanker-derived aggregate estimate outside the main observation window; it does not trace individual cargoes.","review_status":"manually_source_checked_candidate","ground_truth":false},{"id":"O-C17","subject":"oil-malacca","predicate":"served_import_market","object":"oil-china","evidence_ids":["O-S11"],"kind":"estimated_trade_share","source_as_of":"2025-H1","valid_from":"2025-01-01","valid_to":"2025-06-30","recorded_on":"2026-09-22","statement":"EIA estimated that China accounted for 48% of import volumes passing through the Strait of Malacca in the first half of 2025.","caveat":"An aggregate destination share; it does not mean every Chinese crude import used Malacca or identify a cargo, supplier, or refinery.","review_status":"manually_source_checked_candidate","ground_truth":false},{"id":"O-C18","subject":"oil-suez-sumed","predicate":"connected_route_with","object":"oil-bab","evidence_ids":["O-S12"],"kind":"reported_structure","source_as_of":"2025-H1 baseline","valid_from":null,"valid_to":null,"recorded_on":"2026-09-22","statement":"The Suez Canal and SUMED corridor connects Red Sea oil movements with the Mediterranean, while Bab el-Mandeb connects the Red Sea with the Gulf of Aden.","caveat":"A structural route relationship, not evidence that every shipment transits both chokepoints.","review_status":"manually_source_checked_candidate","ground_truth":false},{"id":"O-C19","subject":"oil-cape-good-hope","predicate":"alternative_to","object":"oil-bab","evidence_ids":["O-S12"],"kind":"reported_alternative_route","source_as_of":"2025-H1 baseline","valid_from":null,"valid_to":null,"recorded_on":"2026-09-22","statement":"EIA identifies the Cape of Good Hope as a longer alternative used by some vessels avoiding Bab el-Mandeb and Suez.","caveat":"The graph records route availability, not a vessel track, capacity guarantee or quantified diverted volume.","review_status":"manually_source_checked_candidate","ground_truth":false},{"id":"O-C20","subject":"oil-sunda","predicate":"alternative_to","object":"oil-malacca","evidence_ids":["O-S13"],"kind":"reported_alternative_route","source_as_of":"2025-H1 baseline","valid_from":null,"valid_to":null,"recorded_on":"2026-09-22","statement":"EIA identifies the Sunda Strait as a smaller alternative route around the Strait of Malacca.","caveat":"Alternative status does not establish practical capacity, vessel suitability or actual use in this window.","review_status":"manually_source_checked_candidate","ground_truth":false},{"id":"O-C21","subject":"oil-lombok","predicate":"alternative_to","object":"oil-malacca","evidence_ids":["O-S13"],"kind":"reported_alternative_route","source_as_of":"2025-H1 baseline","valid_from":null,"valid_to":null,"recorded_on":"2026-09-22","statement":"EIA identifies the Lombok Strait as a smaller alternative route around the Strait of Malacca.","caveat":"Alternative status does not establish practical capacity, vessel suitability or actual use in this window.","review_status":"manually_source_checked_candidate","ground_truth":false},{"id":"O-C22","subject":"oil-myanmar-china-pipeline","predicate":"provides_alternative_supply_route_to","object":"oil-china","evidence_ids":["O-S13"],"kind":"reported_infrastructure","source_as_of":"2025-H1 baseline","valid_from":null,"valid_to":null,"recorded_on":"2026-09-22","statement":"EIA identifies the Myanmar–China oil pipeline as an alternative that transports Middle Eastern crude to southwest China outside the Malacca sea route.","caveat":"The source establishes the corridor, not its operating throughput, spare capacity or use for a particular cargo.","review_status":"manually_source_checked_candidate","ground_truth":false},{"id":"O-C23","subject":"oil-us","predicate":"held_commercial_stocks_of","object":"oil-crude","evidence_ids":["O-S14"],"kind":"official_statistic","source_as_of":"week ending 2026-09-11","valid_from":"2026-09-05","valid_to":"2026-09-11","recorded_on":"2026-09-22","statement":"EIA reported U.S. commercial crude oil stocks (excluding the Strategic Petroleum Reserve) at 423.4 million barrels for the week ending September 11, 2026, 1% above the five-year average.","caveat":"A single weekly survey snapshot, not a period average; the five-year comparison set is 2021-2025.","review_status":"manually_source_checked_candidate","ground_truth":false},{"id":"O-C24","subject":"oil-us","predicate":"operates_refining_capacity_of","object":"oil-crude","evidence_ids":["O-S17","O-S18"],"kind":"official_statistic","source_as_of":"2026-01-01","valid_from":"2026-01-01","valid_to":"2026-01-01","recorded_on":"2026-09-22","statement":"EIA reported U.S. operable atmospheric crude oil distillation capacity at 18.2 million barrels per calendar day as of January 1, 2026, down about 1% from 18.4 million b/cd on January 1, 2025 after two refinery closures.","caveat":"Nameplate/operable capacity is not the same as actual utilized throughput in a given week.","review_status":"manually_source_checked_candidate","ground_truth":false},{"id":"O-C25","subject":"oil-india","predicate":"imports","object":"oil-crude","evidence_ids":["O-S19"],"kind":"official_statistic","source_as_of":"2026-27 (Apr-Aug, provisional)","valid_from":"2026-04-01","valid_to":"2026-08-31","recorded_on":"2026-09-22","statement":"PPAC reported India''s crude oil imports at 100.7 million tonnes for April-August of fiscal year 2026-27, provisional and subject to revision.","caveat":"A five-month provisional fiscal-year-to-date figure, not a full-year total; quantities are in tonnes and are not converted to barrels.","review_status":"manually_source_checked_candidate","ground_truth":false},{"id":"O-C26","subject":"oil-iraq","predicate":"produces","object":"oil-crude","evidence_ids":["O-S20"],"kind":"reported_estimate","source_as_of":"2026-08","valid_from":"2026-08-01","valid_to":"2026-08-31","recorded_on":"2026-09-22","statement":"IEA estimated Iraqi crude oil production at 3.86 million b/d in August 2026, within an OPEC+ production table published alongside a report of more than 10 million b/d of Gulf output shut in amid heightened security risks.","caveat":"An IEA supply estimate; OPEC''s own secondary-source estimate for the same month can differ in methodology and value.","review_status":"manually_source_checked_candidate","ground_truth":false}],"events":[{"id":"O-E01","event_time":"2025-Q4","precision":"quarter","published_on":null,"source_ids":["O-S01"],"kind":"estimated_baseline","description":"EIA estimated Hormuz oil flows at 21.6 million b/d before the 2026 disruption window."},{"id":"O-E02","event_time":"2026-Q2","precision":"quarter","published_on":null,"source_ids":["O-S01"],"kind":"estimated_disruption","description":"EIA estimated Hormuz oil flows at 4.9 million b/d and Bab el-Mandeb flows at 8.1 million b/d."},{"id":"O-E03","event_time":"2026-04","precision":"month","published_on":"2026-07-08","source_ids":["O-S07"],"kind":"reported_actual","description":"EIA reported record U.S. crude oil and petroleum product exports of 13.6 million b/d."},{"id":"O-E04","event_time":"2026-06","precision":"month","published_on":"2026-07-16","source_ids":["O-S06"],"kind":"official_statistic","description":"China NBS reported crude processing of 51.24 million tonnes, down 17.7% year over year."},{"id":"O-E05","event_time":"2026-08","precision":"month","published_on":"2026-09-09","source_ids":["O-S02"],"kind":"estimated_market_observation","description":"EIA estimated the August Brent spot price average at $91 per barrel."},{"id":"O-E06","event_time":"2026-10","precision":"month","published_on":"2026-09-06","source_ids":["O-S04"],"kind":"announced_policy","description":"Seven OPEC+ participants announced unchanged required production from September into October."},{"id":"O-E07","event_time":"2026-09","precision":"month","published_on":"2026-09-16","source_ids":["O-S14"],"kind":"official_statistic","description":"EIA reported U.S. commercial crude oil stocks at 423.4 million barrels for the week ending September 11, 2026, 1% above the five-year average."},{"id":"O-E08","event_time":"2026-08","precision":"month","published_on":"2026-09-11","source_ids":["O-S20"],"kind":"estimated_disruption","description":"IEA reported more than 10 million b/d of Gulf oil output shut in amid heightened security risks in August 2026, with global oil production down 1.6 million b/d month-on-month to 100.1 million b/d."}],"excluded_assertions":["A graph path through chokepoints proves the route of an individual cargo.","The change in Brent price can be attributed to one cause.","Nameplate bypass capacity equals available or utilized capacity.","Country-level refinery statistics identify a specific receiving refinery.","A production requirement establishes actual output or compliance."],"briefing":{"title":"Oil under constraint: flows, rerouting and demand response","window_start":"2025-07-01","window_end":"2026-06-30","developments_through":"2026-09-10","framing":"A bounded view of how crude moves from production through chokepoints and refineries, and how the 2026 Hormuz disruption coincided with rerouting, demand response and non-Middle-East supply changes.","metrics":[{"id":"O-M01","title":"Strait of Hormuz oil flow","unit":"million barrels per day","description":"Quarterly total crude oil and petroleum liquids estimated through the chokepoint.","source_ids":["O-S01"],"points":[{"period":"2025-Q3","value":21.3,"status":"estimate"},{"period":"2025-Q4","value":21.6,"status":"estimate"},{"period":"2026-Q1","value":14.9,"status":"estimate"},{"period":"2026-Q2","value":4.9,"status":"estimate"}],"caveat":"AIS became especially unreliable after February 2026; EIA supplements and frequently revises the tanker data."},{"id":"O-M02","title":"Bab el-Mandeb oil flow","unit":"million barrels per day","description":"Quarterly total crude oil and petroleum liquids estimated through the chokepoint.","source_ids":["O-S01"],"points":[{"period":"2025-Q3","value":4.6,"status":"estimate"},{"period":"2025-Q4","value":5.4,"status":"estimate"},{"period":"2026-Q1","value":5.6,"status":"estimate"},{"period":"2026-Q2","value":8.1,"status":"estimate"}],"caveat":"A rise is consistent with changed route use but does not trace the same cargoes displaced from Hormuz."},{"id":"O-M03","title":"World total oil supply","unit":"million barrels per day","description":"Quarterly world supply values reported alongside the chokepoint analysis.","source_ids":["O-S01"],"points":[{"period":"2025-Q3","value":108.2,"status":"estimate"},{"period":"2025-Q4","value":103.9,"status":"estimate"},{"period":"2026-Q1","value":96.1,"status":"estimate"},{"period":"2026-Q2","value":99.7,"status":"estimate"}],"caveat":"Global supply is not a direct measure of chokepoint throughput and reflects multiple production changes."},{"id":"O-M04","title":"China crude oil imports","unit":"million barrels per day","description":"Selected period averages showing the high-import baseline and 2026-Q2 decline.","source_ids":["O-S05"],"points":[{"period":"2025 average","value":11.6,"status":"reported"},{"period":"2025-H2","value":12.0,"status":"reported"},{"period":"2026-Q2","value":8.1,"status":"estimate"}],"caveat":"Periods have different lengths; the series illustrates context rather than a continuous quarterly run."},{"id":"O-M05","title":"Selected U.S. supply response","unit":"million barrels per day","description":"Different measures kept side by side: production, total petroleum exports and a full-year production forecast.","source_ids":["O-S07","O-S08"],"points":[{"period":"2026-H1 crude production","value":13.7,"status":"estimate"},{"period":"2026-04 crude + product exports","value":13.6,"status":"reported"},{"period":"2026 full-year crude production","value":13.8,"status":"forecast"}],"caveat":"These points are not one homogeneous series. Exports include crude and petroleum products; the annual production value is a forecast."},{"id":"O-M06","title":"Major maritime oil routes before the disruption window","unit":"million barrels per day","description":"EIA 2025-H1 estimates provide a common structural baseline for selected chokepoints and the Cape route.","source_ids":["O-S10","O-S11","O-S12"],"points":[{"period":"Malacca","value":23.2,"status":"estimate"},{"period":"Hormuz","value":20.9,"status":"estimate"},{"period":"Cape of Good Hope","value":9.1,"status":"estimate"},{"period":"Suez + SUMED","value":4.9,"status":"estimate"},{"period":"Bab el-Mandeb","value":4.2,"status":"estimate"}],"caveat":"A 2025-H1 structural comparison outside the main observation window. Routes can overlap within one voyage, so values must not be summed as unique cargoes."},{"id":"O-M07","title":"U.S. commercial crude oil stocks","unit":"million barrels","description":"Weekly survey snapshots of commercial crude oil inventories excluding the Strategic Petroleum Reserve.","source_ids":["O-S14","O-S15","O-S16"],"points":[{"period":"week ending 2026-06-19","value":412.1,"status":"reported"},{"period":"week ending 2026-07-17","value":411.7,"status":"reported"},{"period":"week ending 2026-09-11","value":423.4,"status":"reported"}],"caveat":"Each point is a single weekly survey snapshot, not a period average, and the three weeks are unevenly spaced. Relative to the EIA five-year (2021-2025) average for its own week, June 19 was 7% below, July 17 was 6% below and September 11 was 1% above."},{"id":"O-M08","title":"U.S. refinery operable crude distillation capacity","unit":"million barrels per calendar day","description":"Annual EIA Refinery Capacity Report figures as of January 1 of each year.","source_ids":["O-S17","O-S18"],"points":[{"period":"2025-01-01","value":18.4,"status":"reported"},{"period":"2026-01-01","value":18.2,"status":"reported"}],"caveat":"Operable/nameplate capacity as of a single annual snapshot date; it is not actual utilized throughput in any given week. The January 2026 figure reflects 130 operable refineries, down two from 2025."},{"id":"O-M09","title":"U.S. refinery utilization rate","unit":"percent of operable capacity","description":"Weekly EIA survey figures for crude oil inputs to refineries as a share of operable capacity.","source_ids":["O-S14","O-S15"],"points":[{"period":"week ending 2026-06-19","value":96.1,"status":"reported"},{"period":"week ending 2026-09-11","value":96.8,"status":"reported"}],"caveat":"Weekly snapshots, not a continuous or period-averaged series; only two weeks within the window are recorded here."},{"id":"O-M10","title":"India crude oil imports","unit":"million tonnes","description":"PPAC fiscal-year import quantities, with the current fiscal year shown as a provisional partial-year figure.","source_ids":["O-S19"],"points":[{"period":"2024-25","value":243.2,"status":"reported"},{"period":"2025-26","value":245.8,"status":"reported"},{"period":"2026-27 (Apr-Aug, provisional)","value":100.7,"status":"estimate"}],"caveat":"Indian fiscal years run April-March; the 2026-27 point covers only five months and is explicitly marked provisional by PPAC pending actuals. Quantities are in metric tonnes and are not converted to barrels."},{"id":"O-M11","title":"Selected OPEC+ member crude oil production, August 2026","unit":"million barrels per day","description":"IEA country-level supply estimates from its OPEC+ production table for a single month.","source_ids":["O-S20"],"points":[{"period":"Saudi Arabia","value":5.97,"status":"estimate"},{"period":"Iraq","value":3.86,"status":"estimate"},{"period":"Russia","value":8.36,"status":"estimate"},{"period":"Iran","value":2.16,"status":"estimate"}],"caveat":"A single-month cross-country comparison, not a time series. These are IEA supply estimates; OPEC''s own Monthly Oil Market Report uses different secondary-source methodology and can report different country values for the same month."}]}},"questions":[{"id":"O-Q01","question":"What changed at the Strait of Hormuz?","expected_answer":"EIA estimates total oil flows fell from 21.6 million b/d in 2025-Q4 to 4.9 million b/d in 2026-Q2. Treat both as revision-prone estimates, especially after AIS reliability deteriorated.","claim_ids":["O-C02"],"status":"authored_acceptance_case_not_executed"},{"id":"O-Q02","question":"Did the same displaced barrels move through Bab el-Mandeb?","expected_answer":"Unknown. Bab el-Mandeb estimates rose to 8.1 million b/d in 2026-Q2, but aggregate flows cannot establish cargo identity or one-for-one rerouting.","claim_ids":["O-C02","O-C03"],"status":"authored_acceptance_case_not_executed"},{"id":"O-Q03","question":"Can Saudi Arabia bypass Hormuz?","expected_answer":"Partly. The East-West pipeline supports exports through Yanbu, but capacity is not the same as available or actual throughput and does not eliminate other route constraints.","claim_ids":["O-C04","O-C05","O-C14"],"status":"authored_acceptance_case_not_executed"},{"id":"O-Q04","question":"Can the UAE bypass Hormuz?","expected_answer":"It has the Abu Dhabi crude oil pipeline outside Hormuz. The pack establishes infrastructure capability, not actual period throughput or spare capacity.","claim_ids":["O-C06","O-C15"],"status":"authored_acceptance_case_not_executed"},{"id":"O-Q05","question":"How did China respond in 2026-Q2?","expected_answer":"EIA estimated crude imports at 8.1 million b/d, while China NBS reported lower June refinery processing. Import, processing and consumption remain distinct measures.","claim_ids":["O-C07","O-C08","O-C09"],"status":"authored_acceptance_case_not_executed"},{"id":"O-Q06","question":"Did U.S. supply replace all disrupted Middle Eastern oil?","expected_answer":"The corpus does not support that conclusion. U.S. production and exports were high, but product definitions differ and no complete substitution accounting is provided.","claim_ids":["O-C10","O-C11","O-C12"],"status":"authored_acceptance_case_not_executed"},{"id":"O-Q07","question":"Did OPEC+ actually produce at the announced October level?","expected_answer":"Unknown in this window. The September release records a required-production decision, not subsequent measured output or conformity.","claim_ids":["O-C13"],"status":"authored_acceptance_case_not_executed"},{"id":"O-Q08","question":"Did the Hormuz disruption cause the entire Brent price change?","expected_answer":"The sources describe several contributing conditions, but the pack does not identify a single causal share for the price movement.","claim_ids":[],"status":"authored_acceptance_case_not_executed"},{"id":"O-Q09","question":"Which Chinese refinery received a particular cargo?","expected_answer":"Unknown. Country-level customs and processing data do not identify a receiving refinery or trace an individual cargo.","claim_ids":["O-C07","O-C08","O-C09"],"status":"authored_acceptance_case_not_executed"},{"id":"O-Q10","question":"Why does the briefing end observations in June but include September developments?","expected_answer":"June 2026 is the latest common observed endpoint across the selected quarterly and national datasets. Later releases add estimates, forecasts and policy announcements, which remain separately labelled.","claim_ids":["O-C02","O-C07","O-C10","O-C13"],"status":"authored_acceptance_case_not_executed"},{"id":"O-Q11","question":"What alternatives exist around Malacca and the Red Sea?","expected_answer":"EIA identifies Sunda and Lombok as smaller maritime alternatives around Malacca, the Myanmar–China crude pipeline as another supply corridor to southwest China, and the Cape of Good Hope as a longer route avoiding Bab el-Mandeb and Suez. The pack does not establish spare capacity or actual use for a particular cargo.","claim_ids":["O-C19","O-C20","O-C21","O-C22"],"status":"authored_acceptance_case_not_executed"},{"id":"O-Q12","question":"Were U.S. crude oil stocks unusually low in 2026?","expected_answer":"It varied within the window: EIA reported stocks 7% below the five-year average for the week ending June 19 and 6% below for July 17, but 1% above that average by September 11. A single trajectory of ''low stocks'' does not hold across the whole period; each figure is a weekly snapshot, not a period average.","claim_ids":["O-C23"],"status":"authored_acceptance_case_not_executed"},{"id":"O-Q13","question":"Which OPEC+ members were producing the most crude oil in August 2026?","expected_answer":"Among the four IEA reported, Russia (8.36 million b/d) and Saudi Arabia (5.97 million b/d) were highest, then Iraq (3.86 million b/d) and Iran (2.16 million b/d). These are IEA''s own single-month supply estimates, published alongside a report of over 10 million b/d of Gulf output shut in; OPEC''s Monthly Oil Market Report can show different values for the same countries and month.","claim_ids":["O-C26"],"status":"authored_acceptance_case_not_executed"},{"id":"O-Q14","question":"How does India''s oil demand compare to China''s over the same window?","expected_answer":"Unknown from this pack in directly comparable terms. India''s PPAC reports crude imports in million tonnes by Indian fiscal year (April-March), while China''s EIA-derived figures are in million barrels per day by calendar quarter; the pack does not convert units or align the two countries'' periods, so the two series must not be read as a like-for-like comparison.","claim_ids":["O-C25","O-C07"],"status":"authored_acceptance_case_not_executed"}],"answer_mode":"curated_reading_guide"}'::jsonb,
    fingerprint = '78737252b9cde3fb9b7d5bccd294bc2ea38ede096e68fd8726dc53b453b0ae08' WHERE case_id = 'oil-system-2025q3-2026q2';
ALTER TABLE investigation_seed ENABLE TRIGGER seed_immutable;
